ov  7 00:32 global_memory_recent.json\n-rw------- 1 agent agent    7662 Nov  7 00:32 global_memory_summary.md\n-rw-r--r-- 1 agent agent    9025 Nov  7 00:50 iclr2026_conference.sty\ndrwxr-xr-x 2 agent agent    4096 Nov  7 01:13 literature\n-rw-r--r-- 1 agent agent   12373 Nov  7 01:17 memory.md\n-rw-r--r-- 1 agent agent     375 Nov  7 01:11 panel_table.tex\n-rw-r--r-- 1 agent agent     456 Nov  7 01:11 panel_table.tex.prov.json\n-rw-r--r-- 1 agent agent   11070 Nov  7 01:15 paper.aux\n-rw-r--r-- 1 agent agent    7609 Nov  7 01:15 paper.bbl\n-rw-r--r-- 1 agent agent     917 Nov  7 01:15 paper.blg\n-rw-r--r-- 1 agent agent   26973 Nov  2 14:28 paper.bst\n-rw-r--r-- 1 agent agent   14814 Nov  7 01:15 paper.fls\n-rw-r--r-- 1 agent agent   21461 Nov  7 01:15 paper.log\n-rw-r--r-- 1 agent agent    4944 Nov  7 01:15 paper.out\n-rw-r--r-- 1 agent agent  264134 Nov  7 01:15 paper.pdf\n-rw-r--r-- 1 agent agent    8934 Nov  2 14:28 paper.sty\n-rw-r--r-- 1 agent agent   43344 Nov  7 01:19 paper.tex\n-rw------- 1 agent agent 1164242 Nov  7 01:17 paper_agent_codex_20261107_003238.log\n-rw------- 1 agent agent 2045727 Nov  7 00:32 paper_data.json\ndrwx------ 5 agent agent    4096 Nov  7 01:24 paper_diagnostics\n-rw------- 1 agent agent       0 Nov  7 00:32 paper_diagnostics_20261107_003238_35581.log\n-rw------- 1 agent agent   13817 Nov  7 01:24 paper_events_20261107_003238.jsonl\n-rw------- 1 agent agent   21628 Nov  7 01:24 paper_evidence_audit.json\n-rw------- 1 agent agent     272 Nov  7 01:24 paper_evidence_audit.md\n-rw------- 1 agent agent  466355 Nov  7 01:23 paper_evidence_audit_agent_codex_20261107_003238.log\n-rw------- 1 agent agent     944 Nov  7 01:24 paper_evidence_audit_feedback.json\n-rw------- 1 agent agent     959 Nov  7 01:24 paper_evidence_audit_feedback.md\n-rw-r--r-- 1 agent agent   21001 Nov  7 01:19 paper_evidence_audit_input_sha256.json\n-rw-r--r-- 1 agent agent   69865 Nov  7 01:19 paper_evidence_audit_packet.md\n-rw------- 1 agent agent    6588 Nov  7 01:19 paper_evidence_audit_prompt.md\n-rw------- 1 agent agent     232 Nov  7 01:24 paper_evidence_audit_raw.txt\n-rw------- 1 agent agent     791 Nov  7 00:32 paper_prep_20261107_003238.json\n-rw------- 1 agent agent   73231 Nov  7 00:46 paper_prompt.md\n-rw------- 1 agent agent       0 Nov  7 01:24 paper_repair_agent_codex_20261107_003238_round_1.log\n-rw------- 1 agent agent   77551 Nov  7 01:24 paper_repair_prompt_round_1.md\n-rw-r--r-- 1 agent agent   27853 Nov  7 00:45 paper_strategy.json\n-rw-r--r-- 1 agent agent   20070 Nov  7 00:45 paper_strategy.md\n-rw------- 1 agent agent  360291 Nov  7 00:46 paper_strategy_agent_codex_20261107_003238.log\n-rw------- 1 agent agent   47970 Nov  7 00:38 paper_strategy_prompt.md\n-rw------- 1 agent agent     331 Nov  7 00:46 paper_strategy_resolution.json\n-rw-r--r-- 1 agent agent     119 Nov  7 01:14 paper_tools_requirements.txt\n-rw-r--r-- 1 agent agent    8756 Nov  7 00:35 reference_query_plan.json\n-rw-r--r-- 1 agent agent    9435 Nov  7 00:35 reference_query_plan.md\n-rw------- 1 agent agent 1282584 Nov  7 00:36 reference_query_plan_agent_codex_20261107_003238.log\n-rw------- 1 agent agent   33007 Nov  7 00:32 reference_query_plan_prompt.md\n-rw------- 1 agent agent     265 Nov  7 00:36 reference_query_plan_validation_feedback.json\n-rw------- 1 agent agent     279 Nov  7 00:36 reference_query_plan_validation_feedback.md\n-rw------- 1 agent agent    3532 Nov  7 00:38 reference_retrieval.log\n-rw------- 1 agent agent    6837 Nov  7 01:13 references.bib\n-rw------- 1 agent agent   19326 Nov  7 01:13 references_provenance.json\n-rw-r--r-- 1 agent agent    4192 Nov  7 01:13 replay_checks.py\n-rw-r--r-- 1 agent agent    2523 Nov  7 01:13 replay_report.json\n-rw-r--r-- 1 agent agent     374 Nov  7 01:13 replay_report.json.prov.json\ndrwxr-xr-x 2 agent agent    4096 Nov  7 01:12 reproduction_task\nlrwxrwxrwx 1 agent agent      16 Nov  7 00:32 results -> ../investigation\n-rw-r--r-- 1 agent agent    7184 Nov  7 01:13 retrieve_permitted.py\ndrwxr-xr-x 3 agent agent    4096 Nov  7 01:24 scientific-evidence\n-rw-r--r-- 1 agent agent     963 Nov  7 01:11 seed_table.tex\n-rw-r--r-- 1 agent agent     455 Nov  7 01:11 seed_table.tex.prov.json\ndrwxr-xr-x 2 agent agent    4096 Nov  7 01:03 source_evidence\n-rw------- 1 agent agent     265 Nov  7 00:46 strategy_validation_feedback.json\n-rw------- 1 agent agent     271 Nov  7 00:46 strategy_validation_feedback.md\nlrwxrwxrwx 1 agent agent       7 Nov  7 00:32 task -> ../task\n-rw------- 1 agent agent    2611 Nov  7 01:24 validation_feedback.json\n-rw------- 1 agent agent    1817 Nov  7 01:24 validation_feedback.md\n-rw-r--r-- 1 agent agent   27026 Nov  7 01:24 validation_report.json\n# ICLR 2026 Venue Brief\n\nUse this brief to tailor the manuscript for the International Conference on Learning\nRepresentations 2026 submission.\n\n## Hard Constraints\n- Target venue: ICLR 2026.\n- Submission type: conference paper.\n- Body-page budget: 8 to 9 pages, excluding references. A body of 8 pages counts only when its final page is at least 75% full; a shorter or sparser body fails validation.\n- Review model: double-blind. The submission must be fully anonymized.\n- Omit author names, affiliations, acknowledgements, and funding statements from the manuscript.\n- Do not include self-identifying links such as personal repositories, lab pages, or internal URLs.\n- Refer to your own prior work in the third person; never write phrasing that reveals authorship.\n- Include a separate `LLM Usage` section, which may appear in the appendix, describing the precise role\n  of LLMs in research ideation and writing. Significant LLM use must be disclosed; nondisclosure can\n  cause desk rejection.\n- The paper must satisfy the ICLR template and formatting rules selected by `--paper-format iclr`.\n\n## Audience\n- Machine learning researchers working on representation learning, optimization, architectures, and\n  empirical methodology.\n- Readers expect a clearly stated contribution, honest baselines, controlled comparisons, ablations\n  that isolate the mechanism, and explicit statements of scope and limitations.\n- Reviewers reward reproducibility and calibrated claims far more than headline numbers.\n\n## Framing Priorities\n- Lead with the research question and the specific claim the evidence supports.\n- State the contribution precisely in the abstract and introduction: what is new, what it improves,\n  and under which conditions.\n- Motivate the method mechanistically. Explain why it should work, not only that it does.\n- Support the central claim with controlled comparisons against meaningful baselines.\n- Use ablations to attribute the gain to the proposed component rather than to incidental changes.\n- Report variance across seeds or runs whenever the artifacts provide it.\n- Be explicit about the regime studied and where the result is not expected to hold.\n\n## Manuscript Guidance\n- Prefer a title and abstract that name the mechanism and the setting, not a generic improvement claim.\n- In the introduction, make the contribution list concrete and verifiable against the artifacts.\n- In the method section, give enough detail to reimplement: objective, architecture, and the\n  hyperparameters that matter.\n- In the results section, foreground controlled comparisons, ablations, sensitivity, and failure modes.\n- Include a limitations discussion that a reviewer would otherwise raise.\n- Figures must meet top-tier conference standards in both design (clean typography, consistent colors,\n  proper labels and legends, high resolution) and scientific content (clear message, no filler).\n- The template is single-column: size figures for the full text width and keep axis labels legible.\n\n## Anti-Goals\n- Do not deanonymize the submission in any way.\n- Do not overclaim generality beyond the settings actually evaluated.\n- Do not present a benchmark delta as a mechanistic insight without evidence connecting the two.\n- Do not omit baselines or ablations that the grounded artifacts already support.\n- Do not describe results as state of the art unless the comparison in the artifacts establishes it.\n- Do not pad the paper to fill the page budget.\n\n## Decision Rule\n- When venue framing and grounded evidence conflict, follow the grounded evidence.\n- Use this brief to choose emphasis, terminology, and narrative framing, not to invent stronger claims\n  than the run supports.\n{\n  \"agentic_evidence_audit\": {\n    \"checked\": true,\n    \"finding_count\": 0,\n    \"findings\": [],\n    \"summary\": \"Main-paper and supplementary claims match the current evidence, including final qualification, measured comparisons, conditional uncertainty, and implementation limitations.\",\n    \"verdict\": \"pass\"\n  },\n  \"evidence_validation\": {\n    \"bundle_path\": \"work/results/t06/codex/20261106_231454/paper/scientific-evidence\",\n    \"bundle_present\": true,\n    \"checked\": true,\n    \"dangling\": [],\n    \"errors\": [],\n    \"paper_token_count\": 106,\n    \"summary\": {\n      \"anchored_references\": 76,\n      \"dangling_references\": 0,\n      \"manifests_checked\": 8,\n      \"resolved_references\": 30,\n      \"total_references\": 106\n    },\n    \"verification_report_path\": \"work/results/t06/codex/20261106_231454/paper/scientific-evidence/verification-report.json\"\n  },\n  \"generated_at\": \"2026-11-07T01:24:01.307683+00:00\",\n  \"hard_errors\": [\n    \"figure validation failed: figures[1] figure_type does not match strategy for final_disruption_comparison; figures[2] figure_type does not match strategy for paired_effect_uncertainty\"\n  ],\n  \"ok\": false,\n  \"page_validation\": {\n    \"body_pages\": null,\n    \"checked\": false,\n    \"errors\": [],\n    \"exclude_references\": false,\n    \"last_body_page_counted\": null,\n    \"last_body_page_fill_ratio\": null,\n    \"last_body_page_number\": null,\n    \"max_body_pages\": null,\n    \"min_body_pages\": null,\n    \"min_last_body_page_fill_ratio\": null,\n    \"paper_format\": null,\n    \"reference_start_page\": null,\n    \"supplement_pages\": 0,\n    \"supplement_start_page\": null,\n    \"total_pages\": null\n  },\n  \"paper_dir\": \"work/results/t06/codex/20261106_231454/paper\",\n  \"pdf_path\": null,\n  \"soft_warnings\": [\n    \"figures[1] PNG width too small: 1650 < 2400\",\n    \"figures[2] PNG width too small: 1650 < 2400\"\n  ],\n  \"supplementary_information_validation\": {\n    \"appendix_present\": true,\n    \"checked\": true,\n    \"clearpage_present\": true,\n    \"errors\": [],\n    \"heading_present\": true,\n    \"placed_after_references\": true,\n    \"pre_bibliography_clearpage_present\": true,\n    \"rendered_checked\": false,\n    \"rendered_heading_present\": false,\n    \"rendered_visible_character_count\": 0,\n    \"substantive_element_count\": 7,\n    \"visible_character_count\": 9476\n  }\n}# Paper validation feedback\n\n- generated_at: 2026-11-07T01:24:01.307683+00:00\n- paper_dir: `work/results/t06/codex/20261106_231454/paper`\n- ok: `False`\n\n## Hard errors\n- figure validation failed: figures[1] figure_type does not match strategy for final_disruption_comparison; figures[2] figure_type does not match strategy for paired_effect_uncertainty\n\n## Supplementary Information validation\n- appendix_present: `True`\n- heading_present: `True`\n- placed_after_references: `True`\n- pre_bibliography_clearpage_present: `True`\n- clearpage_present: `True`\n- visible_character_count: `9476`\n- substantive_element_count: `7`\n- rendered_checked: `False`\n- rendered_heading_present: `False`\n- rendered_visible_character_count: `0`\n\n## Evidence validation\n- bundle_path: `work/results/t06/codex/20261106_231454/paper/scientific-evidence`\n- bundle_present: `True`\n- verification_report: `work/results/t06/codex/20261106_231454/paper/scientific-evidence/verification-report.json`\n- total_references: `106`\n- resolved_references: `30`\n- anchored_references: `76`\n- dangling_references: `0`\n- manifests_checked: `8`\n\n## Agentic evidence audit\n- checked: `True`\n- verdict: `pass`\n- finding_count: `0`\n- summary: Main-paper and supplementary claims match the current evidence, including final qualification, measured comparisons, conditional uncertainty, and implementation limitations.\n\n## Soft warnings\n- figures[1] PNG width too small: 1650 < 2400\n- figures[2] PNG width too small: 1650 < 2400\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
